# wave flux
# 
# SN Helios (RXC J0018.5+1626, z=3.34) empirical SN II SED template v2
# rest wavelength [A]   F_lambda [arbitrary, peak-normalised]
#   <1000 A        : zero
#   1000-2410 A    : Nugent SN IIP shape (from v1), matched at 2410 A
#   2410-3018 A    : SNANA SN IIP 2004hx, +28.5 d, host CCM E(B-V)=0.16 (from v1)
#   NB the prism does reach rest 1264 A; it is replaced below 3018 A because the
#   binned S/N there is only +2.9 (2410-3018 A), +1.8 (2000-2410 A), +0.8 (<2000 A),
#   too low to carry a template shape. Both model pieces are inherited from v1
#   unchanged and were not re-derived here. Synthetic check at z=3.34: the template
#   gives F090W/F277W=0.0001, F115W=0.004, F150W=0.06, at or below the observed limits.
#   3018-11500 A   : JWST/NIRSpec PRISM, SN Helios (13.1 ks, 2026-08-17), fnu->flam
#   11500-12618 A  : linear prism -> 1999em blend (removes the seam step)
#   12618-25127 A : SN 1999em VLT/ISAAC 1999-11-28, 0.98-2.53 um (Hamuy et al. 2001,
#                    ApJ 558, 615; their Table 2). That paper phases it as 30 d after
#                    discovery; relative to B max it is ~+26 d, against +27.5 d for SN Helios.
#                    Telluric gaps
#                    interpolated, 40 A boxcar, scaled to the prism over 9816-12618 A
#   >25127 A      : blackbody tail, T=4732 K fitted to the 1.6-2.5 um continuum
# No IGM attenuation applied. n=3483
